==Summary==
This is a template for displaying word wall text and their translations. All text should be entered in Roman characters; Dragon text will be converted automatically. Individual lines should be separated with <nowiki><br></nowiki>.

==Parameters==
{{Parameters
|wordwall1<br>wordwall2<br>wordwall3|required|The untranslated word wall text. If all three words are on the same wall, you only need to enter <tt>wordwall1</tt>; otherwise, all three parameters are required.
|translation1<br>translation2<br>translation3|required|The translated word wall text. As with the word wall parameters, only the first is required if all three words are on the same wall.
|shout|optional|Should only be specified if displaying a word wall somewhere other than the related shout's page, such as the example below. Data will not be saved to the page for loading by other pages if this is specified.
}}

==Example==
{{Pre|<nowiki>{{WordWall
|shout=Dismay
|wordwall1   =NONVUL BRON DahMaaN DaaR ROT DO FIN<br> FODiiZ BORMah {{FC|blue|FaaS}} NI BRENDON DO<br> DINOK Fah ROK LOS QOLaaS DO MORO<br> ahRK HIN aaK Wah LOT SOVNGARDE
|translation1=Noble Nord, remember these words of the<br> hoar father: {{FC|blue|Fear}} not (the) specter of<br>death, for he is (the) herald of glory<br> and your guide to great Sovngarde.
|wordwall2   =HET NOK KOPRaaN DO SONaaN<br> ROMERIUS WO UNT {{FC|blue|RU}} NOL OSOS<br> GOGIL NUZ MOTMah
|translation2=Here lies the body of Bard<br> Romerius who tried to {{FC|blue|run}} from some<br> Goblins but slipped
|wordwall3   =QETHSEGOL VahRUKIV DaaNIK<br> FahLiiL KiiR DO GRAVuuN FROD<br>WO BOVUL KO {{FC|blue|MaaR}} NOL KINZON<br> ZahKRii DO KRUZiiK HOKORON
|translation3=This stone commemorates the doomed<br> Elf child of Autumn Field<br>Who fled in {{FC|blue|terror}} from the sharp<br> Sword of an ancient enemy
}}</nowiki>}}
